WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.086 --> 00:00:18.211
As the days Tom started getting used to being king.

2
00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:23.453
He still wasn't comfortable in the role, and he was sometimes homesick.

3
00:00:25.254 --> 00:00:29.716
But he accepted that everyone had to bow to him and that getting dressed was a group project.

4
00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:35.291
Dining in public was supposed to begin on the fourth day of Tom's reign.

5
00:00:39.473 --> 00:00:41.935
That morning he had a meeting with his advisers.

6
00:00:43.516 --> 00:00:47.659
Lord Hertford was talking about important matters, and Tom should have been listening.

7
00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.962
But he was in a bad mood because he was dreading lunch.

8
00:00:51.982 --> 00:00:57.626
"Everyone will be watching me and whispering about me," he thought.

9
00:00:57.646 --> 00:00:59.948
"What if I make a mistake?"

10
00:01:02.849 --> 00:01:05.891
Tom's thoughts were interrupted by the sound of shouting outside.

11
00:01:07.052 --> 00:01:10.054
Eager for any distraction, he jumped up from the table.

12
00:01:11.795 --> 00:01:14.337
He ran to the window but couldn't see anything.

13
00:01:17.979 --> 00:01:20.120
wonder what's going on," Tom said.

14
00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.263
"I'll send a messenger to find out," Lord Hertford said.

15
00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:31.028
A few minutes later, the messenger returned.

16
00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:37.822
"A crowd is following three people—a man plus a woman and her daughter," the messenger said.

17
00:01:37.842 --> 00:01:40.463
"They've been sentenced to death."

18
00:01:42.463 --> 00:01:43.163
"To death?"

19
00:01:43.623 --> 00:01:44.304
Tom said.

20
00:01:44.324 --> 00:01:46.284
"Bring them here.

21
00:01:47.225 --> 00:01:50.485
I want to hear what they've done to deserve such an awful punishment."

22
00:01:54.967 --> 00:01:58.708
The three doomed prisoners soon arrived, accompanied by a sheriff.

23
00:02:00.168 --> 00:02:02.850
As they knelt before Tom, he studied their faces.

24
00:02:06.853 --> 00:02:09.835
something familiar about that man," Tom thought.

25
00:02:09.855 --> 00:02:14.658
"I feel like we've met before, but that's impossible."

26
00:02:16.399 --> 00:02:18.861
He asked the sheriff what the man was accused of doing.

27
00:02:19.861 --> 00:02:22.463
The sheriff looked serious as he answered the question.

28
00:02:22.483 --> 00:02:26.065
"This criminal poisoned a man to death."

29
00:02:27.706 --> 00:02:29.688
Startled, Tom turned to the man.

30
00:02:30.792 --> 00:02:31.572
"Is this true?"

31
00:02:31.592 --> 00:02:34.774
"No, Your Majesty.

32
00:02:35.854 --> 00:02:37.995
The evidence against me is very weak."

33
00:02:39.756 --> 00:02:41.096
"I'd like to hear that evidence.

34
00:02:41.637 --> 00:02:51.201
Sheriff?" "Three witnesses say this man—a stranger—entered a house where another man lay sick in bed," the sheriff

35
00:02:51.221 --> 00:02:54.522
began. "It was ten o'clock in the morning.

36
00:02:55.723 --> 00:02:58.644
The sick man was alone at the time and sleeping.

37
00:03:00.076 --> 00:03:04.340
This man soon left the house, and the sick man died within the hour."

38
00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:09.624
"Did anyone see this man give poison to the sick man?"

39
00:03:09.964 --> 00:03:10.845
Tom asked.

40
00:03:12.466 --> 00:03:14.308
"Was any poison ever found?"

41
00:03:14.328 --> 00:03:16.870
"No, Your Majesty."

42
00:03:18.752 --> 00:03:20.653
Tom scratched his head and looked puzzled.

43
00:03:20.673 --> 00:03:23.816
"Then how do you know he was poisoned?"

44
00:03:27.052 --> 00:03:30.934
"The doctors said his symptoms could only be caused by poisoning.

45
00:03:31.854 --> 00:03:37.997
And there's more: A while ago a witch told several people that the man would be poisoned.

46
00:03:38.857 --> 00:03:43.379
And The sheriff took a deep breath for dramatic effect.

47
00:03:43.399 --> 00:03:47.621
"That a stranger would give the poison!"

48
00:03:49.902 --> 00:03:51.242
Tom was not impressed.

49
00:03:51.262 --> 00:03:54.584
"Most of the world is made up of strangers."

50
00:03:57.452 --> 00:04:02.056
"That's true," one of Tom's advisers whispered to Lord Hertford, who nodded in agreement.

51
00:04:03.837 --> 00:04:06.259
"Yes, Your Majesty," the sheriff said.

52
00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:13.586
"But the witch said that the stranger would have brown hair and wear plain clothing just like this

53
00:04:13.666 --> 00:04:17.509
man." It was hard for Tom to argue with that.

54
00:04:17.529 --> 00:04:21.012
"What do you have to say for yourself?"

55
00:04:21.472 --> 00:04:22.553
Tom asked the man.

56
00:04:22.573 --> 00:04:25.876
"Can any of your friends speak on your behalf?"

57
00:04:28.352 --> 00:04:29.673
"No, Your Majesty."

58
00:04:30.554 --> 00:04:31.635
The man looked sad.

59
00:04:31.655 --> 00:04:37.460
"As you've already heard, I'm a stranger here, so I have no friends.

60
00:04:38.741 --> 00:04:45.626
But if I may speak in my own defense Tom nodded to grant him permission.

61
00:04:45.646 --> 00:04:50.590
"I'm accused of poisoning a man.

62
00:04:51.751 --> 00:04:55.234
But at that exact moment, I wasn't taking a life.

63
00:04:56.735 --> 00:04:59.621
In fact I was saving a life!

64
00:05:01.022 --> 00:05:07.946
A boy was drowning—" Tom held up his hand for silence because he suddenly recognized this man.

65
00:05:07.966 --> 00:05:12.068
"He's the one who pulled Julian from the river!"

66
00:05:12.528 --> 00:05:13.189
Tom thought.

67
00:05:13.209 --> 00:05:15.710
"But I have to be sure."

68
00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:20.213
"On what date is he accused of committing this crime?"

69
00:05:20.593 --> 00:05:21.834
Tom asked the sheriff.

70
00:05:23.495 --> 00:05:25.756
"Well, that's easy for me to remember."

71
00:05:26.976 --> 00:05:28.977
The sheriff puffed up his chest with pride.

72
00:05:30.018 --> 00:05:31.839
"It was New Year's Day!"

73
00:05:31.859 --> 00:05:36.601
"The same day that Julian almost drowned!"

74
00:05:37.041 --> 00:05:37.722
Tom thought.

75
00:05:37.742 --> 00:05:41.244
"Let the prisoner go free!

76
00:05:42.444 --> 00:05:43.745
It is the king's will!"

77
00:05:44.145 --> 00:05:44.926
Tom shouted.

78
00:05:44.946 --> 00:05:50.168
"That other man may have been poisoned, but it wasn't by this man."

79
00:05:54.071 --> 00:05:56.512
Tom was momentarily embarrassed by his outburst.

80
00:05:57.972 --> 00:05:58.992
But he quickly recovered.

81
00:05:59.013 --> 00:06:05.995
"I'm enraged that a man was sentenced to death based on such ridiculous evidence," Tom went on.

82
00:06:06.015 --> 00:06:10.457
"Such gossip shouldn't even be called evidence."

83
00:06:12.658 --> 00:06:16.380
A low buzz of admiration for Tom's intelligence went around the table.

84
00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:23.062
"The king asked such good questions," one adviser said to another.

85
00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:28.706
"I don't see any signs of illness in the boy," the second adviser said.

86
00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:33.150
Lord Hertford rapped on the table to get the advisers' attention.

87
00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:37.635
"Now let's resume our discussion of the royal stables.

88
00:06:38.116 --> 00:06:41.039
The horses—" "Just a minute," Tom interrupted.

89
00:06:41.059 --> 00:06:45.684
"I want to hear what the other two prisoners have to say!"
